  "id": "Compound::DB00376 - Gene::1133",
  "verbalization": "Trihexyphenidyl, a muscarinic receptor antagonist, is shown to bind to Chrm4, Chrm2, and Chrm3, all of which are involved in G-protein coupled acetylcholine receptor activity. This pathway ultimately leads to the participation of Chrm5 in the same activity. The evidence suggests that Trihexyphenidyl may modulate Chrm5 through a common mechanism involving G-protein coupled acetylcholine receptors. The scores from the paths indicate a consistent interaction pattern, with Trihexyphenidyl's binding to multiple muscarinic receptors leading to a shared downstream effect on Chrm5. The integrated evidence supports a mechanistic link between Trihexyphenidyl and Chrm5, mediated through the G-protein coupled acetylcholine receptor pathway. The observed interactions are consistent with a role in modulating muscarinic receptor function, which could have implications for therapeutic applications targeting this pathway.",
